# 🧠 Lab 08 – Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) Image Classification

> **Machine Learning Laboratory** | Building, training, and evaluating a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) for image classification using TensorFlow and Keras.

---

## 📖 Overview

Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) are among the most widely used deep learning models for computer vision tasks. This laboratory focuses on designing and training a custom CNN for image classification using the dataset prepared in **Lab 07**.

The workflow covers the complete deep learning pipeline, including loading image datasets, designing the CNN architecture, training the model, monitoring its performance, saving the best-performing model, and evaluating classification accuracy using performance metrics.

The laboratory consists of a single Jupyter notebook implementing the complete image classification process.

---

## 🎯 Learning Outcomes

After completing this laboratory, students will be able to:

- Understand the architecture of Convolutional Neural Networks
- Load image datasets using TensorFlow/Keras image generators
- Design a custom CNN architecture
- Compile and train deep learning models
- Monitor training and validation performance
- Save the best-performing model using callbacks
- Evaluate classification performance on unseen data
- Generate confusion matrices and classification reports
- Visualize training history and model accuracy

